    desc:'The western half of the same giant cloud of glowing hydrogen as the North America Nebula, split from it on the sky by the dark lane L933/L935. Its bright edge is an ionisation front being eaten into by ultraviolet light from the region\'s hidden O stars, chiefly the Bajamar Star, though a candidate O star in the Pelican\'s neck may do much of the work, and jets such as HH 555 shoot from the tips of the pillars where new stars are forming.',
