    desc:'A classic H II region: a roughly circular bubble of glowing hydrogen in Cepheus nearly three degrees across, blown and lit by the O-star system HD 206267 at the centre of the young cluster Trumpler 37. Its rim is studded with more than twenty bright-rimmed globules being eroded by the star, the Elephant\'s Trunk the most famous of them, and the red supergiant Mu Cephei, Herschel\'s Garnet Star, sits on its northern edge.',
