    desc:'A bright, young open cluster in Cassiopeia whose two brightest stars form the eyes of the Owl, or of E.T. phoning home, with chains of fainter stars for the outstretched arms. Gaia places its roughly 850 members about 9,100 light years away, though whether the brilliant supergiant Phi Cassiopeiae truly belongs to the cluster is still debated.',
