    desc:'A loose knot of faint stars around the bright blue star 20 Vulpeculae, which Gaia shows is a foreground star about a thousand light years away; the cluster behind it lies roughly five thousand light years off, dimmed by nearly two magnitudes of dust. Herschel logged it on two consecutive nights in 1784, so it carries two NGC numbers, and catalogues still disagree about which stars belong to it.',
