  { id: 'dark', log: 100.3, tag: 'pred', title: 'The Dark Era',
    text: 'Even black holes of a hundred billion Suns are gone by about 10¹⁰⁰ years. If protons decay too, all that is left is thin, cold particles and light in a space still expanding, for as long as dark energy stays as it is today.' }
